<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="dsteps">
      <div class="dstep">
        <div class="dstep-n">01</div>
        <div>
          <h3>We jump on a call and qualify you</h3>
          <p>First thing we do is talk. I want to make sure this actually makes sense for your business before you spend a penny. If your trade, your area or your capacity isn't right for it, I'll tell you straight. I'd rather turn work down than take money for something that won't land.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dstep">
        <div class="dstep-n">02</div>
        <div>
          <h3>We come out and build your content bank</h3>
          <p>Me and a videographer come to you and film your real work: the jobs, the finish, the before-and-afters. That gives us a bank of real footage to run ads from, so your campaigns show actual work, never stock. This is the bit most agencies skip, and it's the bit that makes the ads convert.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dstep">
        <div class="dstep-n">03</div>
        <div>
          <h3>I build the ads and the funnel</h3>
          <p>I write and build the ads, set the hyper-local targeting to your exact area, and hand-code the qualifying funnel that filters out tyre-kickers. Then it goes live. You don't touch a thing, and your ad spend goes direct to Facebook, never through me.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dstep">
        <div class="dstep-n">04</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Leads land on your phone</h3>
          <p>Qualified leads come straight to your phone with the name, number, postcode and job type, and automated follow-up keeps them warm while you're on the tools. You quote, you win the job. I keep the campaigns sharp and the phone ringing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <p><strong>One trade, one area.</strong> I only work with one business per trade in each area. Once your patch is taken for your trade, that's it, I won't run the same ads for your competitor down the road. So if someone else gets in first, you're the one on the outside looking in.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What it costs, plainly</h2>
      <p>Two separate things, kept separate. <strong>Ad spend</strong> goes direct to Facebook, and you set a daily budget you're comfortable with, then turn it up as it works for you. <strong>My fee</strong> is separate and depends on your trade and area, so there's no fixed menu. No retainer, no long contract. If it stops working, you stop.</p>

      <h2>What I need from you</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Access to film your work for the content bank</li>
        <li>A budget you're comfortable with for ad spend</li>
        <li>To reply to leads quickly, so they don't go cold</li>
      </ul>
      <p>That's it. I handle the ads, the funnel, the CRM and the follow-up. You stay on the tools.</p>
    </div>

